CORE
main.py
--unwind 10

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An unannotated empty dict filled with int keys inside a range loop is
modeled correctly: the body pre-scan infers the key/value element
types from the first d[k] = v (key int from the range loop variable,
value int from i * 2) and builds the {} with those types at the
creation site, so distinct int keys aren't lossily coerced to the
dict[str, int] default. Previously this required an explicit
dict[int, int] annotation.
